# Root .dockerignore — docker-compose.yml builds backend/Dockerfile with a
# repo-root build context (needed so that Dockerfile can COPY protocol/,
# which schema_validation.py expects at /protocol/schemas — see that
# Dockerfile's COPY comment). Docker only reads .dockerignore from the
# BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, so this file — not backend/.dockerignore, which is
# now dead — is what actually protects secrets from being baked into an
# image layer. Without the block below, backend/.env (real secrets:
# JWT_SECRET, DATABASE_URL credentials, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, DEEPGRAM_API_KEY,
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, TURN_SECRET) gets baked into an image layer the moment
# a developer follows .env.example's own instructions and creates it —
# recoverable from `docker history`/`docker save` even after a later layer,
# and permanently so if the image is ever pushed to a registry.

backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example

# Defense in depth, security review 2026-08-07: the two rules above are
# what actually matters today (Dockerfile only COPYs backend/ and
# protocol/, and no root-level .env exists) — these unprefixed rules are
# a second layer in case either of those two facts ever changes (e.g. a
# future COPY . . reintroduces the exact class of drift that put
# backend/.env at risk of this before, or a root .env gets created since
# Compose itself would look for one there by convention).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

backend/.venv/
backend/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.mypy_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/tests/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
android/
docs/
infra/
bash.exe.stackdump

# Deliberately NOT excluding *.md anywhere under backend/: tried it
# (security review's LOW/hygiene suggestion), and reverted after it broke
# the image build AND the runtime image in two different, non-obvious
# ways — caught only by actually rebuilding and running the image, not
# by reasoning about the patterns. (1) backend/pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`; hatchling refuses to even build the wheel
# without that file present ("OSError: Readme file does not exist").
# (2) backend/app/agent/prompts/*.md (persona.md, business_rules.md,
# rolling_summary.md) are load-bearing prompt templates ContextBuilder
# reads at process startup, not documentation — voice-worker crashed
# outright on boot without them. A few KB of genuinely-non-sensitive
# README text shipping in the image is a complete non-issue; chasing an
# allowlist for every file this pattern turns out to also match is not
# worth the risk of missing one and silently breaking the service again.
